speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, recently the GVRD, representing 50 per cent of British Columbians, passed the following resolution:
Canada was created by the federation of two linguistic groups from an English or French heritage;
It is important to work toward the goal of a country in which all Canadians, irrespective of their origin, can feel comfortable in every region. This requires respect for minority language rights;
Whereas we live in a period characterized by sharp and sometimes rancorous debate on constitutional language questions which threaten the unity and very existence of the nation;
And it is vitally important at this critical time that all Canadians in positions of leadership speak up in support of those principles which underlie the unity and character of Canada;
Therefore, the greater Vancouver Regional District, the third largest urban community in Canada, strongly supports the linguistic duality of our nation and urges all Canadians from coast to coast to display the tolerance and understanding necessary to the building of Canada as a unified nation and constructive member of both the English speaking and French speaking parts of the world community.
